                    {
                        "translation_id": "e60ef162-8180-4228-b9b5-8ba1fb5fa064",
                        "source_entry_id": "30261efb-4447-3cca-97d4-c92ed39e40d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "66db6984-1514-3cfe-b00f-48f8a5963101",
                        "target_lang_word": "shroom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shroom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6831f06a-3d88-3ddc-bc2d-534151968b26",
                                        "entry_id": "60043752-81a1-307f-948b-24c2cb6c1e05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A magic mushroom: a hallucinogenic fungus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc3b466e-d441-45f4-96e8-06a9f9eeeb14",
                                                "sense_id": "6831f06a-3d88-3ddc-bc2d-534151968b26",
                                                "text": "Dosage: The typical amount of beginner “shroom” dosage ranges from 1.5 grams of dried shrooms for a mild experience, to 3.5 grams for an intense experience."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66f481fe-77a5-357a-bd0d-bf30c300e911",
                                        "entry_id": "60043752-81a1-307f-948b-24c2cb6c1e05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any mushroom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46de499e-6f65-446d-bccb-b4ee069aa751",
                                                "sense_id": "66f481fe-77a5-357a-bd0d-bf30c300e911",
                                                "text": "To determine how much live protein may be occupying a shroom, try this test: […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "998d54c0-6fd4-4dd3-b8ca-68f58667d038",
                                                "sense_id": "66f481fe-77a5-357a-bd0d-bf30c300e911",
                                                "text": "These succulent little shrooms from pop culture scholar Lena Lencek will drive everyone back for seconds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "301be2f7-8cc5-44fb-9826-3f77b403ab1f",
                                                "sense_id": "66f481fe-77a5-357a-bd0d-bf30c300e911",
                                                "text": "Shrooms—and I don’t mean the psychedelic kind—are one of those vegetables that you either love or hate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shroom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80ab5a61-9a6c-3829-916c-dbfed1814d41",
                                        "entry_id": "f44955aa-81a2-3cac-bcc1-4f175e95eb88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take magic mushrooms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80cb7ff4-8aad-447d-820b-6a5c172de4c7",
                                                "sense_id": "80ab5a61-9a6c-3829-916c-dbfed1814d41",
                                                "text": "Not just because it was sophmoric^([sic]) and juvenile (which it surely was) but I was shrooming pretty heavily by now."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "174a0d80-0894-414a-a7c2-dd7b355f28d4",
                                                "sense_id": "80ab5a61-9a6c-3829-916c-dbfed1814d41",
                                                "text": "Just a few months ago I was in Amsterdam with two old friends from the Lahore art world. On a warm summer night we checked out some galleries and walked along the canals, whirring bicycles and shrooming teenagers passing us in the darkness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93c54706-fc21-4a83-bf99-4bcae2529357",
                        "source_entry_id": "30261efb-4447-3cca-97d4-c92ed39e40d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "66db6984-1514-3cfe-b00f-48f8a5963101",
                        "target_lang_word": "champignon magique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "champignon magique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63717885-80cd-37ab-ac4e-c7aa6cf0eb6f",
                                        "entry_id": "efa23d30-92bb-35b1-94ea-bbc92f7e17ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonyme de psilocybe lancéolé (espèce de champignons)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f15912b-e50f-4914-ae79-a750ddf2a99a",
                                                "sense_id": "63717885-80cd-37ab-ac4e-c7aa6cf0eb6f",
                                                "text": "Le psilocybe, « champignon magique » du Mexique et de l’Amérique centrale a, dans l’histoire des drogues, un passé plus ancien que toute autre plante dotée d’effets psychiques (opium excepté)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17597468-d2d5-43c7-bff2-877f95598a83",
                                                "sense_id": "63717885-80cd-37ab-ac4e-c7aa6cf0eb6f",
                                                "text": "La victime ne présentait pas d’antécédents médicaux ou psychiatriques particuliers. Selon ses amis, le jeune homme avait déjà consommé des champignons magiques, moyen pour lui de vaincre sa timidité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7a45795-67a3-415a-87b0-ba0546479a15",
                        "source_entry_id": "30261efb-4447-3cca-97d4-c92ed39e40d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "66db6984-1514-3cfe-b00f-48f8a5963101",
                        "target_lang_word": "champignon à psilocybine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "717e9937-12a0-4988-838b-9cf29899537c",
                        "source_entry_id": "30261efb-4447-3cca-97d4-c92ed39e40d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "66db6984-1514-3cfe-b00f-48f8a5963101",
                        "target_lang_word": "champi",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "champi",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1369a5c1-a0f8-3f0b-8988-3bdc773acbb8",
                                        "entry_id": "d2ba6e8c-3ab1-30f3-a275-15a028be6ce9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Champignon hallucinogène."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar",
                                            "neologism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ee5c45a-99bc-4673-8bf0-df5d5ff7c219",
                                                "sense_id": "1369a5c1-a0f8-3f0b-8988-3bdc773acbb8",
                                                "text": "Les champis en thérapie, ou quand planer soigne"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "champi",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5cf7fb9-8fe5-31ce-bdbb-e29ddf7b85a0",
                                        "entry_id": "599de8b3-16d5-33e9-9476-5762f090f7cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Enfant abandonné, bâtard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09343643-da23-43b2-ab1e-cbd7cc8d8088",
                                                "sense_id": "a5cf7fb9-8fe5-31ce-bdbb-e29ddf7b85a0",
                                                "text": "François le Champi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea4afc57-5c19-4114-945b-f20ab6605524",
                                                "sense_id": "a5cf7fb9-8fe5-31ce-bdbb-e29ddf7b85a0",
                                                "text": "— Je t’arrête au titre. « Champi » n’est pas français.\n— Je te demande bien pardon, répondis-je. Le dictionnaire le déclare vieux, Mais Montaigne l’emploie, et je ne prétends pas être plus Français que les grands écrivains qui font la langue. Je n’intitulerai donc pas mon conte François l’Enfant-Trouvé, François le Bâtard, mais François le Champi, c’est à dire l’enfant abandonné dans les champs, comme on disait autrefois dans le monde, et comme on dit encore aujourd’hui chez nous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d95653e-7b09-45e7-98f5-a87949df8d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "a5cf7fb9-8fe5-31ce-bdbb-e29ddf7b85a0",
                                                "text": "Enfin, un brave petit champi, « gardeux d’oueilles » (bon petit cœur), qui me voulait du bien, parce que je l’avais surpris une fois picorant mes cerises et que je lui avais dit : « Beau merle, pendant que tu y es, cueilles-en aussi pour moi », se faufila près de la fenêtre, écouta et cria :\n— Monsieur Breugnon, j’y vas !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "005d5ffe-b349-3ad4-8592-416f78e0654e",
                                        "entry_id": "599de8b3-16d5-33e9-9476-5762f090f7cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de papier pour les châssis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
